# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings
#
# Every tracked file in this repository is text today (there is no binary
# asset yet). Without this file, a checkout's line endings depend on the
# checking-out machine's `core.autocrlf`: a Windows machine or CI runner with
# `core.autocrlf=true` (a common default, including this project's own
# development machine and GitHub's windows-latest runner) converts every
# blob's LF endings to CRLF on checkout. Prettier is configured for `lf`
# (`.prettierrc.json`, `.editorconfig`) and does not follow `core.autocrlf`,
# so a CRLF checkout makes `npm run format:check` fail on every text file —
# not because any file's content actually changed, but because the checkout
# step silently rewrote every line ending before Prettier ever looked at it.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide per file whether it is text; `eol=lf` fixes the
# checked-out line ending to LF regardless of the checking-out platform's
# `core.autocrlf`, so every clone and every CI runner sees the same bytes
# Prettier already expects.
* text=auto eol=lf
